# Night report lines. GameState.events plays one cue per event, in order.
# Each event's values are passed in, so {{name}}, {{amount}} etc. work.
# Lines with no "Name:" are narration. Keep each line under ~70 characters.
# Use % for random variations, like in visitors.dialogue.

# poor_harvest: {{amount}} = meals per gardener tonight, {{total}} = what the whole garden made,
# {{name}} = a gardener who was working (to blame).
~ poor_harvest
% Maggots were seen on the farm, infested crops had to be thrown out
% The soil was tired, the harvest came up thin
%
	Temperatures on the plot fell below zero,
	{{name}} could only come up with {{amount}} meals
% {{name}} didn't make an effort to irrigate the plot properly
%
	{{name}} tripped and fell while working the plot
	they only managed to produce {{amount}} meals tonight
% {{name}} spotted a scarecrow eating away at vegetables at the plot
%
	{{name}} reported newly grown vegetables present a weird color
	unsure if they are edible, they threw this night's batch out
=> END

# garden: {{amount}} = meals made, {{gardeners}} = how many worked the plots, {{name}} = one of them.
~ garden
if gardeners == 1
	% The garden gave {{amount}} meals.
	% One pair of hands on the plot. {{amount}} meals.
	% Working hard on the farm, {{name}} produced {{amount}} meals
else
	% The garden gave {{amount}} meals.
	% {{gardeners}} gardeners brought in {{amount}} meals.
	% {{gardeners}} worked together to produce {{amount}} meals tonight
=> END

# forager_returned: {{name}}, {{amount}} = meals, {{materials}} = materials, {{food}} = pantry after their haul (before dinner).
~ forager_returned
if food <= 5
	%
		Luckily, {{name}} came back with much needed supplies
		Enough for {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	% Thankfully, {{name}} is back with {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	%
		{{name}} is back from the hunt with some animal meat
		You are not quite sure what it is, but the situation is dire
else
	%2 {{name}} came back from their journey with {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	%2 {{name}} made it home unscathed, carrying {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	%
		{{name}} is back. The glimmer in their eyes is gone; the wilderness is not for everyone.
		Luckily, the search was not fruitless. {{name}} brought the farm {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials.
	%
		Seems the residents of the farm will be having a hearty meal.
		{{name}} came back with {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	%
		{{name}} came back tonight. Around the dinner table, they told stories of the outside world.
		It seems the disease is spreading with no end in sight.
		Despite it all, they brought back enough food for {{amount}} meals and {{materials}} materials
	%
		{{name}} has arrived on the farm, dirt on their clothes.
		They found a cattle farm not far away, the cattle roaming with no one to care for them.
		The residents of the farm will be eating steak tonight.
=> END

~ forager_lost
% {{name}} never came back from the road.
% There's no sign of {{name}}. They aren't coming back.
% {{name}} has likely not survived the Washington wilderness
% Two days have passed since {{name}}'s departure, with no signs of life
% {{name}} has not made it back.

=> END

~ eaten
Everyone was fed. {{amount}} meals gone, {{left}} left.
=> END

~ died
% {{name}} didn't wake up this morning.
% {{name}} is gone.
=> END

~ infected
% {{name}} was by {{from}}'s side at the end. Now they're sick too.
% {{name}} has the same cough {{from}} had.
%
	{{from}}'s body was found by {{name}}
	{{name}}'s eyes have become yellow
=> END

~ no_guard
No one kept watch last night.
=> END

~ farm_full
The farm is full. No one else can be let in.
=> END

~ slipped_in
% {{name}} slipped in while everyone slept.
%
	Through a hole in the electric fence, a new resident has entered
	{{name}} has apologized for the damage, promising to work on the farm
%
	A new person appeared on the farm.
	{{name}} somehow climbed the electric fence, with bruised hands to show for it
=> END

~ lost_starved
The last of the food is gone.
=> END

~ lost_alone
You are the only one left.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Cure
# researched: one random line per researcher, every night they research.
# research_0/25/50/75: how it feels, played after the researched lines every research night.
# research_breakthrough: the night research first reaches 100%.
# research_ready: any later night someone still researches.

~ researched
% {{name}} spent the night buried in old textbooks.
% {{name}} stayed up scribbling notes by candlelight.
% {{name}} pored over medical journals until dawn.
% {{name}} ran another round of experiments in the shed.
=> END

~ research_0
You feel lost in the material, swarmed with no understanding in sight.
=> END

~ research_25
You feel like you’ve come to grasp the basics of chemistry and human biology.
However, you’re far from finding a cure.
=> END

~ research_50
You are starting to feel more confident in your knowledge.
An end might be in sight.
=> END

~ research_75
It’s only a matter of weeks before you reach a breakthrough.
You are starting to feel hope.
=> END

~ research_breakthrough
BREAKTHROUGH! You have the knowledge on how to synthesize the cure!
You can now send one of your residents to acquire the correct chemicals from the old EPA building.
A trip back and forth will take 4 days, and is very dangerous.
But a successful one will end this nightmare.
=> END

~ research_ready
You can now send one of your residents to acquire chemicals for the cure.
=> END

~ lab_returned
{{name}} made it back from the old EPA building with the chemicals!
=> END

~ lab_lost
{{name}} never came back from the EPA building.
=> END

# synthesizing: {{nights}} done so far out of {{total}}.
~ synthesizing
{{name}} worked on the cure through the night. ({{nights}}/{{total}})
=> END

~ synthesis_interrupted
The work on the cure was interrupted. It will have to start over.
=> END

~ cure_done
{{name}} finished the cure.
It works. This nightmare is over.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hidden attributes
# food_stolen: a greedy resident took food. Never name them. {{amount}} = meals taken.
~ food_stolen
% Some food went missing from the pantry overnight.
% The pantry looks lighter than it should. {{amount}} meals are gone.
=> END

# fight: a fight where nobody died. {{a}} and {{b}} are in random order (don't reveal who started it).
~ fight
% {{a}} and {{b}} got into a fight last night.
% Shouting woke the farm. {{a}} and {{b}} came to blows.
=> END

# fight_killed: {{killer}} killed {{name}}.
~ fight_killed
% {{killer}} killed {{name}} in a fight.
% A fight broke out. {{name}} didn't get up. {{killer}} was standing over them.
=> END

# infected_by_fight: {{name}} (the killer) caught it from {{from}} (the sick victim).
~ infected_by_fight
{{name}} got {{from}}'s blood on their hands. Now they're sick too.
=> END

# infected_bystander: {{from}} was a sick superspreader killed in a fight; {{name}} caught it too.
~ infected_bystander
{{name}} was there when {{from}} fell. Now they're sick too.
=> END

~ ration_needed
There is not enough food to feed everyone. {{count}} resident(s) must go without.
=> END

~ bed_built
% {{name}} spent the night hammering and sawing. The farm now has an extra bed!
% Working through the night, {{name}} managed to construct a new bed using the scavenged materials.
=> END

~ starved
% {{name}} went without food for too long and didn't make it through the night.
% Weakened from hunger, {{name}} passed away.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tattletale
# After a theft or a fight nobody died in, someone may point a finger.
# Half the time it's true, half the time it's the culprit lying. The culprit is always
# either {{accuser}} or {{accused}}: never say which, that's the player's puzzle.

# tattle_theft: {{accuser}} says {{accused}} has been stealing food.
~ tattle_theft
% {{accuser}} pulled you aside. They say {{accused}} has been stealing food.
% {{accuser}} swears they saw {{accused}} sneaking out of the pantry.
=> END

# tattle_fight: {{accuser}} says {{accused}} started the fight.
~ tattle_fight
% {{accuser}} insists {{accused}} started the fight.
% {{accuser}} says it was all {{accused}}'s doing.
=> END
